course: dictionary
lesson: 14711
title: Proclaimed: announcing and speaking out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Proclaimed» is the past tense of «proclaim», which means to say something loudly and clearly so that everyone can hear. Look at the words around it to find out what kind of speaking is happening.
explain: «The king proclaimed a holiday.» This is official: a ruler announced something to the whole country. «"I won!" she proclaimed.» Here it means she said it loudly and proudly, as if she wanted the whole world to know.
explain: Stories often use «proclaimed» instead of «said» to show how a character feels. «Self-proclaimed» is a little different: it means someone calls themselves something, but there may be no proof. Check the clues before you believe a title.
fact: Proclaim means to announce something publicly, or to say it loudly and proudly.
fact: «Proclaimed» means announced or said loudly and clearly, as in «The king proclaimed a new law».
fact: «Self-proclaimed» means someone calls themselves something, often without proof: «a self-proclaimed expert».
fact: In church, a preacher proclaims God's message, meaning they speak it out to the people listening.
fact: Said is a plain word; proclaimed shows the speaker is proud, loud or official.
exercise: «The mayor proclaimed that the school would close for a holiday.» What does proclaimed mean here? | Whispered quietly to a friend | Drew a picture of it | *Officially announced to everyone | Forgot to say it
exercise: «"I scored the winning goal!" he proclaimed, arms in the air.» What does proclaimed show? | *He was loud and proud | He was scared of the ball | He was whispering a secret | He was tired and sleepy
exercise: Mia reads that a man is a «self-proclaimed expert» on dinosaurs. What does self-proclaimed suggest? | He is a dinosaur | He has won a prize for dinosaurs | *He calls himself an expert, but there may be no proof | He is a real scientist with many books
test: «The queen proclaimed a new law for the whole kingdom.» Which word is closest in meaning to proclaimed? | Hid | Argued | *Announced | Forgot
test: In church, the preacher proclaimed God's word. What is the preacher doing? | Singing a quiet song alone | Counting the people in the hall | *Speaking God's message to the people | Falling asleep in the front row
exam: Which sentence shows someone speaking loudly and proudly? | Sam stayed silent all day. | *«We made it to the top!» Sam proclaimed. | «Pass the salt,» Sam whispered quietly. | «Pass the salt,» Sam mumbled.
